  "doc.title": "Where the Power Comes From the Instant You Flip the Switch · A Hands-On Long-Form Essay",
  "doc.desc": "The grid stores almost nothing, so generation must match use every instant. Ten models you can push: inertia and frequency, governors, a day as grid operator, high-voltage line loss, the transformer, three phases, merit-order prices, the duck curve, storage and a cascading blackout.",
